FROM (VALUES
  ('15935e49-5d60-467e-8864-ca7177769dd0','Pinehurst Archery in Pinehurst, North Carolina is a USA Archery affiliated club running both Junior Olympic Archery Development and Adult Archery Programs, backed by an on-site 3D course and lessons for people just getting started. That combination, youth and adult pathways plus a 3D course and instruction, makes it one of the more fully built-out clubs in the area, capable of serving a family across age groups and skill levels. Pinehurst''s national reputation as a golf destination brings a fair amount of outside visitor traffic to the region too, which could make a club like this a stop for traveling archers as well as locals. Anyone interested in JOAD enrollment, adult lessons, or 3D shooting should reach out directly for current scheduling.'),
  ('dfa809f7-209a-4e2f-a172-ce454b6d8cfc','Pioneer Sportsmen JOAD operates in Dunbarton, New Hampshire as a USA Archery affiliated club with both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program running side by side. Sportsmen''s clubs in rural New England towns like Dunbarton often combine multiple outdoor disciplines under one roof, and this one has clearly built out a formal, nationally affiliated youth archery pathway alongside its adult offering rather than treating archery as an afterthought. South-central New Hampshire doesn''t have an abundance of structured JOAD programs, so a club like Pioneer Sportsmen fills a real gap for families in the area. Parents or adults interested in either program should contact the club directly for enrollment details and current schedule.'),
  ('2b91f9f7-aa43-4680-a79a-fc9381072f74','Pivot Archery, based in Decatur, Georgia just east of Atlanta, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. Decatur''s dense, walkable inner-ring suburb setting is a bit different from the more rural clubs that dominate Georgia''s archery scene, suggesting Pivot likely serves an urban and suburban Atlanta clientele rather than a hunting-focused rural membership. Running JOAD and adult programs together means the club can serve a whole family rather than just kids or just grown-ups. For archers in the Atlanta metro looking for a structured, USA Archery-affiliated club close to the city rather than out in the exurbs, Pivot Archery is worth a direct inquiry.'),
  ('3e97dbd5-e657-4b2d-b37d-20dbf5d35225','Podium JOAD, based in Paris, Kentucky, is a USA Archery affiliated club whose programs span Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, and 3D archery instruction, giving it one of the broader program lineups among Kentucky''s JOAD clubs. Paris sits in the heart of the Bluegrass region''s horse country, and a club offering this range of programming, youth, adult, and 3D-style shooting, gives local archers options beyond a single narrow focus. The name Podium signals competitive ambitions consistent with USA Archery''s structured pathway toward tournament shooting. Families or adult archers in the Bourbon County area looking for a program that covers both target archery development and 3D-style instruction should reach out directly for enrollment and schedule details.'),
  ('26eb9cfa-31af-4893-a4f3-0370639413e2','Poweshiek County Sportsmen''s Association in Montezuma, Iowa runs as a volunteer club with an ASA affiliation, which puts it in the 3D archery and bowhunting-style scoring circuit that a lot of rural Iowa clubs use to organize their season. Montezuma sits in farm country in the eastern half of the state, the kind of area where a sportsmen''s association often doubles as a hub for hunting-minded archers beyond just archery itself. Diane Henry is listed as a contact, a good first call for anyone wanting to know shoot schedules, course access, or membership terms, since day-to-day operating details for a volunteer group like this typically aren''t posted anywhere public.'),
  ('89c11f9b-fc6b-4cea-922d-c76b8dede616','In Dodge City, Kansas, Prairie Bowman Archery Club Inc. operates as a volunteer-run club carrying an ASA affiliation, tying it into the same 3D archery and bowhunting-oriented circuit found across much of the plains states. Dodge City''s western Kansas location sits in strong hunting territory, and a club like this typically serves as the local gathering point for archers who want realistic target rounds ahead of deer or turkey season. Travis Stalkfleet is the listed contact, worth reaching out to for shoot dates, course conditions, or how to join, since a volunteer operation like this rarely keeps posted hours or a public schedule beyond word of mouth among members.'),
  ('09f364cf-32d5-4f69-bde3-1ccc065cc0b6','Prairie Bowmen Archery Club in Lincoln, Nebraska is a USA Archery affiliated club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, which makes it one of the state capital''s better options for kids and teens looking for a structured path into competitive target archery. The club also offers lessons and has a 3D course on-site, so it isn''t purely an Olympic-style operation, it also caters to archers interested in more realistic, hunting-style rounds. Lincoln''s size gives it enough of an archery community to support a club running both a youth pipeline and adult instruction. Anyone wanting to enroll a junior archer or book a lesson should contact the club directly for current scheduling and fees.'),
  ('10a2f652-6b44-41f5-a25d-69dbc99f4f09','Predator''s Archery JOAD in Gilroy, California runs a USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program, putting it among the South Bay''s options for young archers wanting a structured, competition-oriented path rather than casual shooting. Gilroy sits south of San Jose in an area with a fair amount of outdoor recreation activity, and a dedicated JOAD program here gives local families a nearby option instead of driving further north into the Bay Area proper. Nothing beyond the JOAD affiliation is listed for this club, no pro shop or lesson specifics beyond the program itself, so parents interested in enrolling a young archer should contact the club directly for session times and costs.'),
  ('c9d33ef0-f033-4a14-9265-cd03ce2a7695','Pro Line Archery Lanes in Ozone Park, Queens runs a USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program, giving New York City families in this part of the borough a nearby option for structured youth archery instruction rather than having to travel to a suburban club. Queens is dense and short on outdoor space, so an indoor lanes-style setup running a JOAD program fills a real gap for city kids wanting a legitimate path into competitive archery. Beyond the JOAD affiliation, no other program or amenity details are listed here, so parents or young archers interested in joining should contact Pro Line directly to ask about session times, age groups, and cost.'),
  ('e038ccbc-eddc-40b3-80dd-c22891733566','Quails Run Archery Club LLC in Eustis, Florida is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club, placing it in the same hunting-style scoring circuit used by clubs across the Southeast. Eustis sits in the Lake County area of central Florida, a region with a decent amount of both target archery and bowhunting activity given the mix of lakes, farmland, and hunting land nearby. The club''s LLC structure suggests a more formally organized operation than a purely informal group, though it still runs as a volunteer club rather than a public commercial range. Ron Quails is listed as the contact, the right person to reach for shoot dates, course access, and membership details not posted elsewhere.'),
  ('22136ea6-050f-48f8-a014-30e6c00c1a2c','Quest Archery in Worcester, Massachusetts is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, plus an on-site pro shop and lessons, making it one of central Massachusetts''s more complete archery operations spanning multiple age groups. Worcester is the state''s second-largest city, and having youth and adult programming under one roof alongside a retail shop suggests a club built to serve a whole family rather than a single niche of shooter. That combination of instruction, programming for two age groups, and gear on-site is a genuine step above a bare range. Anyone interested in either program should contact Quest directly for schedules, pricing, and current openings.'),
  ('7c86aece-7264-490d-b44b-f1dbe8762fa6','R&D 3D Archery is based in Milner, a small community south of Atlanta in Georgia''s Lamar County, and runs a 3D course as its listed feature, a realistic-target style of archery favored by hunters honing shot judgment before deer season. Its ASA affiliation status is recorded here as expired for 2025, so anyone relying on that affiliation for sanctioned shoots or scoring should confirm the club''s current status directly rather than assume it''s still active. Middle Georgia has a solid rural hunting base that supports clubs built around 3D courses like this one. Beyond the course itself, no other program details are listed, so a direct call is the way to get current information.'),
  ('0849cfa8-717e-4d87-9dbf-bfbdc5558cbc','Rancho Park Archers is a USA Archery affiliated club on the west side of Los Angeles running an Adult Archery Program along with lessons, a solid entry point for grown adults in the city who want structured instruction rather than figuring out the sport on their own. Los Angeles has a big enough population to support a range of archery options, but a club specifically built around adult programming, rather than youth-focused JOAD, fills a more specific niche for career-age beginners and returning archers. Rancho Park itself is a well-known recreational area on LA''s west side, giving the club a central, accessible location. Anyone interested should contact the club for current session times and fees.'),
  ('0e9fd69f-8077-46e8-a527-a5365638f046','Ravlin Hill Archery is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in Panama, a small town in far western New York near the Pennsylvania and Ohio borders. That corner of the state has a solid rural hunting base, and an ASA affiliation ties this club into the same 3D scoring and course-style shooting used by clubs across the region for bowhunters keeping their distance judgment sharp. Daniel Burkholder is listed as the contact, a good starting point for anyone wanting to know shoot dates, course conditions, or membership details, since a small volunteer club like this typically doesn''t publish a set schedule anywhere beyond word of mouth among local members.'),
  ('fdb93c2f-ea71-4529-b2c5-875a087bb210','Razorback Archery is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in Ash Flat, a small town in the Ozark foothills of north-central Arkansas. That region''s rugged, wooded terrain makes it prime bowhunting country, and an ASA affiliation puts this club in the same realistic-target, hunting-oriented scoring circuit used by clubs throughout the Ozarks. David Gibson is the listed contact, a useful first call for anyone wanting to know about upcoming 3D shoots, course access, or how to become a member, since day-to-day details for a small volunteer club like this generally aren''t posted publicly. Ash Flat''s rural setting and hunting culture make a club like Razorback a natural gathering point for local archers.'),
  ('15aeb423-ad76-4942-b039-abb25448d9fa','RBD Known Triple Classic is listed as an archery club in Gillet, a small community in Bradford County in Pennsylvania''s rural northern tier, close to the New York border. Its name suggests ties to a specific tournament or shoot format, likely a known-distance 3D event, rather than a standard club title. Its ASA affiliation status is recorded here as expired for 2025, so anyone planning around that affiliation should confirm the club''s current standing directly rather than assume it''s still active. Northern Pennsylvania''s hilly, forested terrain supports a strong bowhunting culture that a club or event like this would typically serve. Reaching out directly is the way to get current information.'),
  ('72e309d0-f818-4bad-96b0-a5908bc8d7c3','Recon Archers in Denver is a USA Archery affiliated club running an unusually broad slate of programming, Junior Olympic Archery Development for young archers, an Adult Archery Program, plus both 3D and field archery formats, covering nearly every major style of the sport under one club. That range of offerings makes it one of the more comprehensive options in the Denver metro, whether the interest is Olympic-style target shooting, casual adult instruction, or the more hunting-oriented 3D and field formats. Few clubs list this many distinct programs at once, which suggests a genuinely active, multi-generational membership base. Anyone interested in any of these programs should contact Recon Archers directly for current schedules and enrollment details.'),
  ('2af1328e-affc-4587-a975-070152f3cb1b','Red Cedar Archery in Hartland, Michigan runs a USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program alongside an Adult Archery Program, giving this Livingston County community, roughly between Detroit and Lansing, a club serving both younger competitive archers and adults looking for structured instruction. Having both age tiers under one roof suggests Red Cedar functions as a genuine community hub rather than a narrow youth-only or adult-only operation. Hartland''s location along the busy corridor connecting Michigan''s two largest metro areas gives the club a fairly wide catchment of potential members. Anyone interested in enrolling in either program should contact Red Cedar Archery directly to ask about class times, age requirements, and cost.'),
  ('d86e78c4-3461-48aa-992d-2c30384c10ce','Red River Bowhunters Inc is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in Stanton, a small town in the Red River Gorge area of eastern Kentucky, a region well known for its rugged terrain and outdoor recreation. That gorge country supports a strong bowhunting tradition, and the club''s ASA affiliation places it within the realistic-target 3D scoring circuit common among hunting-oriented archers in the Appalachian foothills. David Fannin is listed as the contact, the right person to reach for information on shoot schedules, course conditions, or membership, since a small volunteer club in this kind of rural setting typically doesn''t maintain posted public hours. Reaching out directly is the way to get current, accurate details.'),
  ('e01c6b14-e65f-42d4-a6fe-b640b3ba5fad','Benton, Illinois is close to Rend Lake, and Rend Lake Archery takes its name from the reservoir, running as an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club rather than a commercial range. ASA affiliation puts the club inside a national scoring and competition structure built around foam-animal targets, which tends to draw a bowhunting-minded membership more interested in realistic shot practice than flat-target scoring. Donnie Millenbine is listed as a contact for the club, a practical starting point for anyone wanting to know about shoot schedules, membership requirements, or whether the course is open to visiting archers. Beyond that contact and the ASA affiliation, this listing doesn''t include lane counts or additional amenities, so reaching out directly is the way to get current details.'),
  ('ee22f7bb-ec72-497f-9c8f-65b812a7a85a','Ridge Archers in Lakeland, Florida combines an ASA affiliation with both a 3D course and a field course, giving members two different formats to shoot rather than just one. The 3D side puts foam-animal targets in play for bowhunting-style practice, while a field course adds shots at varying, often uneven distances closer to traditional field archery scoring, a fuller setup than most volunteer clubs offer. Central Florida''s ridge country around Lakeland has a long-running archery and bowhunting community, and a club with two course types tends to be one of the more active hubs in that scene. Maurice Campbell is listed as a contact for questions about membership or scheduling, since this record doesn''t include hours or costs directly.'),
  ('c09243f3-cead-4de2-a556-3d55b3cb9132','Rigneys School of Archery in Glenarm, Illinois is a USA Archery affiliated hybrid facility running three programs at once: Junior Olympic Archery Development for young competitive shooters, an Adult Archery Program, and 3D Archery for those more interested in foam-animal target practice. That range of programming, spanning youth competition, adult participation, and bowhunting-style shooting, makes it a broader operation than a single-purpose club or range, closer to a school that happens to also function as a shooting facility. Central Illinois doesn''t have an overwhelming number of USA Archery affiliated schools, so a JOAD pathway in a small town like Glenarm stands out. Specific class schedules and costs aren''t listed here, so contacting the school directly is the way to get current details.'),
  ('8b0d4064-3be5-445c-b7e4-bf51a0a04df0','Cottonwood sits in Arizona''s Verde Valley, rugged high-desert terrain that gives Rim Country Bowhunters Association its name and likely shapes its bowhunting-focused membership. The club is USA Archery affiliated and runs an Adult Archery Program, which points to organized shooting for grown archers even though the group''s name leans toward hunting rather than pure target competition. That combination, a hunting-oriented club name paired with a formal adult program, suggests members split time between bowhunting prep and more structured target practice. No detail is given here on a 3D course, field course, or lessons for younger archers, so anyone interested in the club''s full range of activities should reach out directly for current information.'),
  ('951c23c8-396b-419a-8128-7ce440095daf','Rising Phoenix Archery in Troy, Michigan, in the northern Detroit suburbs, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, plus lessons for archers looking to learn the basics. Having both a JOAD pathway for younger competitive shooters and a separate adult track, alongside general instruction, makes this a fairly comprehensive setup for a club rather than a narrow, single-audience operation. Oakland County''s suburbs support a decent amount of youth archery activity, and a JOAD club with lessons attached tends to be a starting point for families new to the sport. Costs, class times, and equipment requirements aren''t included in this listing, so contacting the club is the way to get specifics.'),
  ('1aaafd0a-ec59-41ed-9382-b3b2e621156a','Rivanna Archery takes its name from the river running through Charlottesville, Virginia, and operates as a USA Archery affiliated hybrid facility offering both an Adult Archery Program and 3D Archery. Pairing structured adult instruction with a 3D course gives shooters a path from learning fundamentals to practicing on foam-animal targets, useful for anyone easing into bowhunting-style shooting after starting with basic technique. Central Virginia has a fair amount of archery and bowhunting activity, and a USA Archery affiliated club adds a level of standardized instruction that not every local range offers. There''s no mention here of a JOAD program for younger shooters or a dedicated pro shop, so those details would need to come from the club directly.'),
  ('21a96273-609b-40f7-afe7-497794235f43','Franklin, Georgia, a small town near the Alabama line, is home to River Bottom Outdoors, an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club rather than a retail or public range. The ASA affiliation ties the club into a national 3D archery scoring system built around foam-animal targets, a format that tends to appeal to bowhunters looking to sharpen shot placement outside of hunting season. Scott Parrott is the listed contact, a useful point of entry for anyone wanting to know about shoot dates, course conditions, or membership. Western Georgia has a strong bowhunting tradition, and volunteer clubs like this one are often where that local community gathers outside of deer season itself. No further amenities or lane details are listed here beyond the ASA affiliation and contact name.'),
  ('9471a72e-0fcd-4398-9c0c-06c7d787667c','Riverbrook Robins in Wilton, Connecticut runs as a USA Archery affiliated club offering both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, giving it a shooting population that spans young competitive archers and adults learning or refining the same Olympic-style discipline. Fairfield County has a number of well-organized youth sports programs, and a JOAD club in this part of the state fits that pattern, offering a structured path toward regional or national competition for kids who stick with it. The adult program alongside it suggests the club isn''t purely youth-focused, though this listing doesn''t specify class times, costs, or whether a 3D or field course is also available. Reaching out to the club directly would confirm those details.'),
  ('d099c029-f64e-4dbc-b24b-41978a1cf6db','Riverside Archers in Hudson, Massachusetts stacks up a lot in one listing: USA Archery affiliation, a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, an Adult Archery Program, a field course, lessons, and 12 lanes, making it one of the more fully documented clubs in this batch. Twelve lanes alongside a field course means members can shoot both a standard indoor or flat setup and a course laid out at varying, natural distances, while the JOAD and adult programs cover competitive youth and general adult participation side by side. Lessons round it out for total beginners. Central Massachusetts doesn''t have an overwhelming number of clubs this comprehensive, so Riverside Archers looks like a genuine hub for the area. Specific scheduling and pricing still require a direct call to the club.'),
  ('041bda15-8282-4229-9f2b-42de813f5728','Elberton, Georgia, known regionally for its granite industry, is also home to Rock Branch Archery, an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club serving the surrounding Piedmont countryside. The ASA tie-in places the club within an organized national scoring system for foam-animal target shooting, a format popular with bowhunters looking to sharpen range estimation and shot placement outside of hunting season. Bobby McCannon is listed as the club''s contact, the practical route for anyone wanting details on shoot schedules or how to get involved. Northeast Georgia has a steady bowhunting community, and clubs like this one often function as the social and competitive hub for that crowd. No lane counts or additional amenities are noted beyond the ASA affiliation and contact information.'),
  ('95787060-8f35-4f93-85e1-4864723ecdc9','Rock Rapids sits in the far northwest corner of Iowa, and Rock River Archery Club, named for the river running through the area, is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club serving that corner of the state. The ASA affiliation connects the club to a national scoring format built around foam-animal targets, generally appealing to a bowhunting-minded membership rather than pure target archers. Tim Boekhout is the listed contact, a direct route to information on shoot dates, course access, and membership for anyone in the area. Rural northwest Iowa doesn''t have a dense cluster of archery clubs, so Rock River likely serves a fairly wide surrounding area. No lane count or additional amenities are included here beyond the ASA tie and contact name.'),
  ('b20ea0e9-e8ff-4bb9-99c3-74544dafecf1','Rocky Mountain Archery Association in Colorado Springs is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club, tying its membership into a national scoring system built around foam-animal targets rather than flat-target rounds. Colorado Springs sits at the base of Pikes Peak with easy access to national forest land, and an ASA club in this location likely draws a membership focused on bowhunting preparation as much as competitive 3D shooting. Anne Geist is listed as the club''s contact, the direct route for questions on shoot schedules, course conditions, and how to join. No lane count, pro shop, or lesson program is noted in this record, so those details, along with current membership costs, would need to come from the club itself.'),
  ('33aaf0c7-48eb-42fe-8bbc-fa42e0d04495','Rocky Mountain Hot Shots in Fort Collins is a USA Archery affiliated club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, putting its focus on young archers working toward regional and national competition rather than casual or purely recreational shooting. Fort Collins, home to Colorado State University, has a fairly active youth sports scene, and a dedicated JOAD club fits into that pattern as a structured option for families looking for competitive archery specifically rather than a general hobby range. This listing doesn''t mention an adult program, 3D course, or lessons for beginners outside the JOAD track, so parents or older archers interested in other options should contact the club directly to ask what else, if anything, it offers.'),
  ('9e380fd9-1851-4a0e-a8ec-b7081a76cbeb','Monroe, North Carolina, southeast of Charlotte, is home to Rocky River Archery Club, an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club named for the river that runs through the region. ASA affiliation places the club in a national scoring format centered on foam-animal targets, a style that tends to draw bowhunters looking to practice shot placement and range estimation outside of deer season. Rory Wall is listed as the club''s contact, a useful starting point for anyone wanting to know about shoot dates or how to join. The Charlotte area''s southeastern suburbs have a decent-sized bowhunting community, and clubs like this one often serve as a regular gathering point for it. No lane count or facility amenities are noted beyond the ASA tie and contact name.'),
  ('128f5f8b-3637-4d28-8c16-775ce4e1d7c2','Ross County Bowhunters is a volunteer-run 3D archery club based in Chillicothe, Ohio, affiliated with the Archery Shooters Association. That ASA tie places the club squarely in the 3D and bowhunting-practice tradition, where members shoot foam animal targets at varied, unmarked distances to sharpen the same judgment used in the field. Brandon Rowan serves as the listed contact for anyone looking to get involved, ask about membership, or find out when the course is open to visitors. Chillicothe sits in south-central Ohio''s Scioto River valley, an area with a strong bowhunting culture, and clubs like this give local hunters a low-pressure place to practice range estimation and shot placement before season.'),
  ('149f2413-945d-4944-ab24-4fa2f3485bfa','Rub Line Archery is a volunteer 3D archery club in Moneta, Virginia, affiliated with the ASA and built around foam-target shooting at bowhunting-realistic distances. Moneta sits near Smith Mountain Lake in the Virginia foothills, a region with a strong deer-hunting tradition, and a club like this gives local bowhunters somewhere to test range judgment and shot placement outside of season. Hunter Jacobs is listed as the contact for anyone wanting to inquire about joining, visiting the course, or learning when it''s open to the public. As with most volunteer clubs, hours and access likely depend on member schedules, so reaching out ahead of a visit is the reliable way to plan one.'),
  ('790e9803-d4e8-45f7-8c45-5bd3bcd83c52','In Howard City, Michigan, Rustic Archery Shooters Club runs as a volunteer, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club serving the west-central part of the state. The ASA affiliation signals a course built around foam-animal targets at realistic, unmarked distances, the standard format for archers sharpening bowhunting skills between seasons. Jennifer Martindale is the point of contact listed for the club, useful for anyone asking about membership, course conditions, or scheduled shoots. Howard City''s rural Montcalm County setting fits the bowhunting-practice focus well. Because it''s volunteer-run rather than commercial, availability likely tracks member involvement rather than posted business hours, so a call or message ahead of a visit is worth the effort.'),
  ('478f2aee-b462-4a15-a049-3ff5678b9563','SA Xtreme is a USA Archery-affiliated hybrid facility in San Antonio, Texas, running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program for young shooters working toward competitive form and Olympic-style technique. That JOAD pathway is the club''s defining feature, giving families in the San Antonio area a structured, nationally recognized track rather than casual open shooting alone. As a hybrid facility, it likely blends club-style programming with broader public access, though specifics on a pro shop or 3D course aren''t confirmed here. San Antonio''s size makes it a natural hub for organized youth archery in south-central Texas. Parents or archers interested in the JOAD program should contact SA Xtreme directly for enrollment and schedule details.'),
  ('14c57aef-fefc-4d92-b64c-898aabf5b231','Sage Creek Archery is a volunteer, ASA-affiliated 3D club in Mount Airy, North Carolina, near the Virginia line in the state''s northern Piedmont. The ASA connection points to a foam-target course built for bowhunting practice, letting members work on distance judgment and shot placement in a realistic but low-stakes setting. David Smith is listed as the club''s contact for questions about membership or visiting the course. Mount Airy''s surrounding farmland and forest make it solid bowhunting country, and a club like Sage Creek gives local archers somewhere to stay sharp between seasons. Since it''s volunteer-run, reaching David Smith directly is the best way to confirm current shoot times and whether new members are welcome.'),
  ('b136c005-a852-47f9-a85e-da9891c6c675','Salina Bowmen Archery Club, despite the name, is based in Niles, Kansas, and runs as a volunteer, ASA-affiliated club with its own 3D course for bowhunting-style practice. Members shoot foam-animal targets at unmarked, realistic distances, the standard ASA format used to sharpen field judgment ahead of hunting season. Eric Schneweis is the listed contact for anyone wanting to ask about membership, course conditions, or upcoming shoots. Central Kansas'' open plains and strong deer-hunting culture make a club like this a natural community hub for local bowhunters. As with most volunteer clubs, hours likely follow member schedules rather than fixed business hours, so contacting Eric Schneweis ahead of a visit is the reliable path.'),
  ('dc1de057-719c-4390-aa13-485b3fe02270','Salt River Bowhunters is a volunteer, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in Shelbyville, Missouri, in the rolling farmland of the state''s northeast. The ASA affiliation means the course is built around foam-animal targets at bowhunting-realistic, unmarked distances rather than a standard flat range, aimed squarely at hunters keeping their shot judgment sharp. Rusty Hammond is the contact listed for the club, the person to reach for membership questions or details on when the course is open. Shelbyville''s rural setting near the Salt River fits the club''s name and its hunting-focused membership base. Because it''s volunteer-run, prospective members should expect shoot schedules to follow the group''s own calendar rather than posted commercial hours.'),
  ('1ae20943-46f1-444e-aacc-d15cf274ab4f','Salthawk Archery is a volunteer, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in Hutchinson, Kansas, a city known regionally for its salt mines and central-Kansas location. The club''s ASA tie points to a foam-target 3D course designed for bowhunting practice, where members work on judging distance and shot placement the same way they would in the field. Jessica Vaile is listed as the contact for anyone interested in membership or visiting the course. Hutchinson''s surrounding farmland supports a strong hunting community, and a volunteer club like Salthawk gives local archers a dedicated place to train outside of season. Reach out to Jessica Vaile directly for current shoot schedules and membership details, since the club runs on member time, not staffed hours.'),
  ('f94623e0-fe66-4c69-88b5-4d3c8f88a9e8','Saluda River Archery Club in Piedmont, South Carolina, is a USA Archery-affiliated hybrid facility running a full slate of programming: Junior Olympic Archery Development for young competitive shooters, an Adult Archery Program for grown beginners and returning archers, and 3D Archery for those practicing bowhunting-style shots. A pro shop on site handles equipment needs, and lessons are available for anyone starting from scratch, making this one of the more complete stops in the area for archers of any age or experience level. Piedmont sits in the upstate region between Greenville and Anderson, giving the club a decent population base to draw from. Contact Saluda River Archery Club directly for current class schedules and membership options.'),
  ('9d6e0591-c0fc-4e7e-987d-59881c980b11','San Francisco Archers is actually based in Pacifica, California, just south of the city along the coast, and holds USA Archery affiliation with both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. Lessons are available, so the club serves newcomers as directly as it serves kids on the JOAD competitive track. That combination of youth development and adult instruction under one roof gives Bay Area families and adult beginners alike a structured entry point into the sport rather than just open shooting time. Pacifica''s coastal setting adds a scenic backdrop uncommon among inland ranges. Interested archers should contact San Francisco Archers directly for current lesson availability and JOAD enrollment details.'),
  ('91036d97-7daf-4f35-ac7f-13b52443bad9','Sanctuary Archery is a volunteer, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in McAlister, Oklahoma. The ASA affiliation points to a course of foam-animal targets set at realistic, unmarked distances, the format bowhunters use to practice range judgment and shot placement outside of hunting season. Brandon Gray is listed as the contact for the club, the person to reach with questions about membership or course access. Oklahoma''s hunting-heavy rural culture makes a club like Sanctuary a natural community fixture in its area. Because it''s run by volunteers rather than paid staff, shoot times likely follow the group''s own schedule, so reaching Brandon Gray directly is the surest way to plan a visit or ask about joining.'),
  ('9c6efc5a-6874-45e0-a078-44d34ba88e99','Sandune Archery Club, Inc. is based in Myrtle Beach, South Carolina, and has held ASA affiliation with a 3D course for bowhunting-style practice, though the current listing notes that status as expired for 2025. That''s worth flagging honestly rather than glossing over: affiliations lapse and get renewed, so it doesn''t necessarily mean the club or its course is inactive, just that the ASA status on file isn''t current. Myrtle Beach''s coastal location along South Carolina''s Grand Strand gives the club a mix of local and seasonal-resident archers to draw from. Anyone interested in Sandune Archery Club should contact them directly to confirm current affiliation status, course access, and whether membership is currently open.'),
  ('6bfe19b5-7587-4dde-a521-005ce6d4823e','Santa Paula Archery is a USA Archery-affiliated hybrid club in Santa Paula, California, in Ventura County''s agricultural Santa Clara River valley. It runs both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program for young competitive shooters and an Adult Archery Program for grown beginners or returning archers, giving the club a genuine cross-generational reach rather than serving just one age group. That dual-track structure makes it a solid option for families where kids and parents both want structured instruction rather than open shooting time alone. Specifics on a pro shop or 3D course aren''t confirmed here. Interested archers in the Santa Paula or greater Ventura County area should contact the club directly for JOAD and adult-program enrollment details.'),
  ('7836ca2b-23f7-4116-af29-67b2c770941f','Sapphire Mountain Archery is a USA Archery-affiliated hybrid club in Hamilton, Montana, named for the Sapphire Mountains that flank the nearby Bitterroot Valley. The club runs a Junior Olympic Archery Development program alongside an Adult Archery Program, giving both young competitive shooters and adult beginners a structured way into the sport rather than unstructured range time alone. Hamilton''s rural, mountain-valley setting in western Montana comes with a strong outdoor and hunting culture that likely feeds interest in both programs. Specifics on a pro shop or 3D course aren''t confirmed for this listing. Families or adult archers in the Bitterroot Valley should contact Sapphire Mountain Archery directly for current class schedules and enrollment.'),
  ('16b07f12-47db-4b8c-810d-fa1484a48977','Sarasota Archery Academy, also in Sarasota, Florida, is a USA Archery-affiliated hybrid facility running a notably full set of programs: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, and Field Archery. That range covers competitive youth training, adult instruction, bowhunting-style foam targets, and longer-distance field rounds all under one academy, making it one of the more comprehensive stops on Florida''s Gulf Coast for archers regardless of age or discipline. Sharing a city with Sarasota Archers Inc gives local archers two distinct options depending on whether they want a lesson-focused club or this broader academy structure. Contact Sarasota Archery Academy directly for current program schedules, ages served, and enrollment details.'),
