  ('d4abfa83-0dae-4f8c-aa30-3110da5b3804','SeiChu Kyudo Kai in Bellevue, Washington carries a name that nods to the Japanese art of kyudo, and it operates as a USA Archery affiliated club running an Adult Archery Program with lessons available. That combination makes it a natural landing spot for grown-up beginners in the Seattle-area suburbs who want structured instruction rather than just open range time. Being USA Archery affiliated also means the club follows a recognized set of safety and coaching standards rather than operating informally. Anyone curious whether the club leans traditional Japanese-style shooting or Olympic recurve fundamentals, or both, should contact SeiChu Kyudo Kai directly to ask about class format and enrollment.'),
